\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Mass windows and gauge-field index formulas}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{Golterman, Jansen and Kaplan compute the coefficient of an induced Chern–Simons current in odd bulk dimension for small, slowly varying external fields. Their mass-to-Wilson-coupling ratio crosses the even corner thresholds. Their alternating binomial coefficient has the same mass-window dependence as \ref{fdip-019Y} on even periods \citet{v1, Eqs. (9), (12), printed pp. 6–7}{golterman1993chern}. Kaplan's bound mode uses a mass changing sign in an extra dimension \citet{Eqs. (3)–(6), printed p. 3; (7)–(13), printed pp. 4–5}{kaplan1992method}.}

\p{Lüscher expresses the Abelian magnetic flux through a coordinate plane as an integer times #{2\pi} and fixes it within a flux sector \citet{Eqs. (2.9)–(2.11), printed pp. 4–5}{luscher1998abelian}. Hernández, Jansen and Lüscher bound their Wilson-kernel square under a plaquette bound to prove locality of the associated Neuberger operator \citet{Section 2.3, Eqs. (2.15)–(2.16), printed pp. 5–6}{hernandez1998locality}. The angle in \ref{fdip-019X} is taken on a single scalar line: for a scalar phase #{u} acting on a fiber of dimension #{f}, the determinant phase of the represented plaquette is #{u^f}. The two principal arguments can differ even when the latter is zero.}
